 "differences": [
  "In the practice-bout table (LL_Table) the authors' clearance is the absolute value of foot height minus obstacle height (157 rows where the foot was lower than the top of the obstacle show a positive number), whereas in the baseline, catch and retention tables it is signed (negative when lower). foot_clearance_m is the authors' value as shared in each table, so signs are not comparable across them.",
  "Retention_table of 18 control participants lists the first 32 obstacles of the retention test twice (identical obstacle positions and foot heights; the repeat has error 1.0 in the authors' error column, while their undocumented second error column error.1 holds the real value). Both listings are kept; performance_error_alt_m holds error.1. Treat the repeats (the second 32 rows with block 1 and trial numbers 1-32 again) as duplicates in analysis.",
  "Table 1 of the paper gives the control group for 22 participants; the deposit's 20 analysed controls are not comparable to it, so control demographics are not used as checks."
 ],
